86433627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433617 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433619 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433622 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433623 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433625 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1077 "selection" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433622 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433627 1079 #uuid "5ef00e22-7033-5539-a4d7-5c70d771c4f1" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433618 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433620 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433621 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433624 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1075 #edb/ref 17592186433626 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1077 "selection" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1078 #edb/ref 17592186433621 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433628 1079 #uuid "c90f0f81-e6f6-5365-9a31-9800a129aea5" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433627 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433629 1069 "q-80546" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433629 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433629 1071 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)$ given that its derivative ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the corresponding unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)=⟨-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,\\,{T}^{′}(t)=⟨-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433629 1072 #uuid "c48a3e25-1a31-5723-bb94-d587dcc4bb55" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433629 1074 "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{′}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{′}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${T}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))}^{2}+{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2 \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16({sin}^{2}⁡(2t)+{cos}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\,2\\,}{4}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186433628 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433630 1069 "q-64696" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433630 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433630 1071 "Find the curvature at an arbitrary point on the curve $r(t)={t}^{2}\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+t\\,k.$" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433630 1072 #uuid "d3e668b2-3360-5bad-970e-ebd786d68368" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433630 1074 "Let $T(t)$ denote the unit tangent to the given curve as a function of the parameter $t.$ Since we are given the curve $r(t)$ parametrized by the parameter $t$ (not the arc length $s$), we will use the following formula for the curvature: \n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)k \\\\  & =2t\\,i+2t\\,j+1\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{(2t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nHence, the corresponding unit tangent vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}(2t\\,i+2t\\,j+k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNext, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and find its magnitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}})\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}(2\\,i+2\\,j-8t\\,k) \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-8t)^{2}}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8+{8}^{2}{t}^{2}}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8(1+8{t}^{2})}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{(\\frac{\\sqrt{8}\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}})}{\\sqrt{8{t}^{2}+1}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{8}}{{(8{t}^{2}+1)}^{3/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433631 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433632 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433631 1062 #uuid "00d70dc7-07a1-5030-82b3-0ddd637fbfb1" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433631 1063 #edb/ref 17592186433630 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433632 1058 #edb/ref 17592186433633 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433632 1062 #uuid "59cb16be-b5c6-5ba7-9b02-4ee7270ded13" 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [17592186433632 1063 #edb/ref 17592186120495 13194139534712 17592186045417 true] [